%N A164734 Number of n-digit cycles of length 2 under the Kaprekar map A151949.
%C A164734 The 2-cycles are the three families of Theorem 1.2 of Mayne, Shapiro and Van Cott (see Links): {53955, 59994} (n = 5), one family with n = 13+2*j digits (j >= 0), and one family with n = 9*u+7*(p+r) digits (u >= 1, p > r >= 0). According to that paper, Dolan has proved that there are no others. - _Yukihiro Kimura_, Nov 13 2026
%H A164734 Joseph Myers, <a href="/A164734/b164734.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n=1..140</a>
%H A164734 Rebekah Mayne, Quinn Shapiro, and Cornelia A. Van Cott, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.22564">There and back again with Kaprekar 2-cycles</a>, arXiv:2608.22564 [math.NT], 2026.
%H A164734 <a href="/index/K#Kaprekar_map">Index entries for the Kaprekar map</a>
%F A164734 Conjectures from _Chai Wah Wu_, Apr 13 2024: (Start)
%F A164734 a(n) = a(n-7) + a(n-9) + a(n-14) - a(n-16) - a(n-21) - a(n-23) + a(n-30) for n > 41.
%F A164734 G.f.: x*(-x^40 - x^38 - x^36 + x^33 - x^32 + 2*x^31 - x^30 + 2*x^29 - x^28 + x^27 + x^25 - x^24 + 2*x^23 - x^22 + 2*x^21 - 2*x^20 + x^19 - x^16 - x^15 - x^14 + x^13 - x^12 + x^11 - x^4)/(x^30 - x^23 - x^21 - x^16 + x^14 + x^9 + x^7 - 1). (End)
%F A164734 G.f.: x^5 + x^13/(1-x^2) + x^16/((1-x^7)*(1-x^9)*(1-x^14)). The three terms count the three families of 2-cycles described in the Comments. This g.f. equals the one conjectured by Chai Wah Wu above. - _Yukihiro Kimura_, Nov 13 2026
